# =============================================================================
# Auth — LOGOUT requests (VS Code REST Client)
# =============================================================================
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend (http://localhost:4000).
#   2. Run top-to-bottom — chained requests reuse earlier responses.
#
# Notes:
#   - All data is FAKE. Manual probes only; the automated suite is in
#     src/test/java.
#   - Model: logout revokes the access token's jti (in-memory blocklist) and
#     burns the refresh family. Garbage inputs are tolerated as no-ops (204).
#   - Expected codes: 204 logged out / no-op, 400 invalid payload.
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: register Ada (201 or 409 — both fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ada Obi",
  "email": "ada.obi@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234567"
}

### 2 — Setup: login Ada (tokens reused below)
# Expected: 200
# @name oLoginAda
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.obi@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 3 — Valid logout (Bearer access token + refresh token in body)
# Expected: 204 — no content; both halves of the session are revoked
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{oLoginAda.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{oLoginAda.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 4 — Refresh with the burned token from request 3
# Expected: 401 — the family is dead
POST {{baseUrl}}/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{oLoginAda.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 5 — Setup: register + login Bola (garbage-Bearer persona)
# Expected: 201 or 409, then 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Ade",
  "email": "bola.ade@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348055551234"
}

### 6 — Setup: login Bola
# Expected: 200
# @name oLoginBola
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.ade@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 7 — Logout with a GARBAGE Bearer token but a VALID refresh token
# Expected: 204 — the bad access token is ignored (no-op); the valid refresh
# token's family is still burned
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer garbage.token.value
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{oLoginBola.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 8 — Setup: register + login Chidi (no-header persona)
# Expected: 201 or 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Chidi Okafor",
  "email": "chidi.okafor@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "08031234568"
}

### 9 — Setup: login Chidi
# Expected: 200
# @name oLoginChidi
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "chidi.okafor@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 10 — Logout with NO Authorization header, valid refresh token
# Expected: 204 — the header is optional; the refresh family is still burned
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{oLoginChidi.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 11 — Logout with a garbage refresh token (never issued)
# Expected: 204 — tolerated as a no-op; nothing to revoke
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "never-issued-token"
}

### 12 — Empty JSON body
# Expected: 400 — refreshToken is a required field (Bean Validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{oLoginChidi.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 13 — Repeat of request 3 (idempotency — logout twice)
# Expected: 204 — second logout with already-revoked data is a safe no-op
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{oLoginAda.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{oLoginAda.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Revoked access tokens: the logout blocklist matters for PROTECTED routes
# (/api/v1/** beyond auth). None exist yet — the catalog stage will be the
# first place to probe "Bearer revoked token → 401" end to end.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
